Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:07.28,Default,,0,0,0,,The U two example shows why joint integrality differs from separate factor requirements. With b zero equal
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.28,0:00:14.76,Default,,0,0,0,,to one and b one equal to six, the quadratic form is m squared plus m n plus n squared. It is integral for
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.76,0:00:20.99,Default,,0,0,0,,every integer pair. The formal criterion also covers rational coefficients with a common nonzero
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.99,0:00:27.54,Default,,0,0,0,,denominator. This example is not an anomaly free supergravity spectrum.
